end
$do$;

-- Top 3D Visualization Companies: A Map of Who Does What  (en)
do $do$
declare pid uuid;
begin
  select post_id into pid from public.blog_post_translations where locale = 'en' and slug = $v$top-3d-visualization-companies$v$;
  if pid is null then
    insert into public.blog_posts (status) values ('draft') returning id into pid;
  end if;
  update public.blog_posts set
    status = 'published', publish_at = coalesce(publish_at, now()),
    category_id = (select id from public.blog_categories where slug = $v$guides$v$),
    author_id = (select id from public.blog_authors where slug = 'vari-studio'),
    cover = $v$b80319_eaf114bae9ad46aebe7b9c11a9e978c2~mv2.png$v$,
    cover_alt = $v${"en": "Timeless English Roof Architecture, a European-style roofing concept visualized by VARI Studio"}$v$::jsonb,
    faq = $v$[{"q": {"en": "What are the top 3D visualization companies?"}, "a": {"en": "It depends on what you mean. Among studios, recent CGArchitect Studio of the Year winners SALTVISION and Brick Visual stand out. Among software makers, Chaos (V-Ray, Corona, Enscape) and Epic Games (Unreal Engine, Twinmotion) dominate. Directories such as Clutch list hundreds of smaller firms."}}, {"q": {"en": "What does a 3D visualization company do?"}, "a": {"en": "A visualization studio turns drawings and design intent into photorealistic images, animations, virtual tours or interactive experiences, mainly for architects, developers, interior designers and brands."}}, {"q": {"en": "Are directory rankings reliable?"}, "a": {"en": "They are useful for discovery, but some placements are sponsored and reviews vary in depth. Always check a company's own portfolio and ask for a complete series from a similar project."}}, {"q": {"en": "Which software do most visualization studios use?"}, "a": {"en": "Common combinations include 3ds Max with V-Ray or Corona for production stills, and real-time tools such as Unreal Engine, Twinmotion, Lumion, Enscape or D5 Render for animation and interactive work."}}]$v$::jsonb
  where id = pid;
  insert into public.blog_post_translations (post_id, locale, slug, title, excerpt, html, takeaways, seo_title, seo_description, focus_keyword, ready, word_count)
  values
  (pid, $v$en$v$, $v$top-3d-visualization-companies$v$, $v$Top 3D Visualization Companies: A Map of Who Does What$v$, $v$The top 3D visualization companies are not all studios. A map of the industry: award-winning studios, the software makers behind them, and where to find talent.$v$, $v$<p>Ask who the top 3D visualization companies are and you get very different answers depending on who you ask. A developer means the studios that make the images. A visualizer means the companies that make the software. A procurement team means the platforms where you can compare hundreds of suppliers. All three are right, and knowing which kind of company you actually need saves a lot of wasted calls.</p>
<p>Here is the industry, mapped from the people who make the pictures to the tools and marketplaces around them.</p>
<h2>1. Visualization studios: the companies that make the images</h2>
<p>These are the firms you hire for renders, animations and virtual tours. They range from one-person practices to international studios with offices on several continents.</p>
<p>The most reliable independent signal of who leads this group is the annual <strong>CGArchitect 3D Awards</strong>, now presented with Chaos. Their recent Studio of the Year titles went to <strong>SALTVISION</strong> (Belgium) in 2025 and <strong>Brick Visual</strong> (Hungary) in 2024. We cover those results and what they mean in <a href="/en/blog/best-3d-rendering-companies-2026">the best 3D rendering companies in 2026</a>, and the studios recognised over the longer term in <a href="/en/blog/best-architectural-visualization-studios">the best architectural visualization studios</a>.</p>
<p>Because buyers usually choose close to home, we also keep regional guides:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/en/blog/top-3d-visualization-companies-germany">Top 3D visualization companies in Germany</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/top-3d-visualization-studios-europe">Top 3D visualization studios in Europe</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/top-3d-visualization-companies-united-states">Top 3D visualization companies in the United States</a></li></ul>
<p><strong>Choose a studio when</strong> you need finished images, film or interactive work and want one team accountable for the result.</p>
<h2>2. Software makers: the companies behind every render</h2>
<p>Every studio depends on a handful of technology companies. Their names appear constantly in the industry, and knowing them helps you read proposals and portfolios.</p>
<p><strong>Chaos</strong> makes V-Ray and Corona, two of the most widely used production renderers, and Enscape, a real-time renderer that runs inside design software. Chaos and Enscape merged in 2022, and Chaos now also presents the CGArchitect 3D Awards.</p>
<p><strong>Epic Games</strong> makes Unreal Engine, used for interactive sales tools and VR, and Twinmotion, a real-time visualization tool. Epic's licence page says Twinmotion is free for companies with annual revenue up to US$1 million.</p>
<p><strong>Act-3D</strong> develops Lumion, a real-time renderer popular for placing buildings in rich landscapes.</p>
<p><strong>Autodesk</strong> makes 3ds Max, long a standard modelling platform in visualization studios, as well as Revit, where many architectural models start.</p>
<p><strong>The Blender Foundation</strong> stewards Blender, the free and open-source 3D suite that many freelancers and small studios now use.</p>
<p>We compare the tools in <a href="/en/blog/best-rendering-software-for-architecture">the best rendering software for architecture</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Choose software when</strong> visualization is something your own team will do regularly.</p>
<h2>3. Marketplaces and directories: where companies are listed</h2>
<p>When people search for a list of visualization companies, they often land on directories. They are useful for breadth, but read them with care.</p>
<p><strong>Clutch</strong> lists hundreds of firms in its 3D rendering category, with client reviews. Some placements are sponsored. <strong>GoodFirms</strong> publishes reviewed lists of rendering companies. <strong>CAD Crowd</strong> is a freelance network that also publishes "top companies" lists by country and speciality. Portfolio platforms such as <strong>Behance</strong> and the project pages on <strong>ArchDaily</strong> let you judge work directly.</p>
<p><strong>Use directories when</strong> you want to see many options quickly. Then verify each name on its own website and portfolio, because a listing is not an endorsement.</p>
<h2>4. In-house teams: the visualization departments inside firms</h2>
<p>Many large architecture practices and developers run their own visualization departments. You will not hire them, but they matter: they set the quality bar that outside studios are compared against, and they often outsource peaks of work to specialist studios. If you are such a firm, our guide to <a href="/en/blog/outsourcing-architectural-rendering">outsourcing architectural rendering</a> covers how that relationship works.</p>
<h2>Which kind of company do you need?</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Your situation</th><th>The company you need</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A launch, competition or planning submission needs finished images</td><td>A visualization studio</td></tr><tr><td>Your team renders weekly for design reviews</td><td>Software (and training)</td></tr><tr><td>You want to compare many suppliers quickly</td><td>A directory, then verify</td></tr><tr><td>You have steady demand and occasional peaks</td><td>In-house plus an outsourcing partner</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Where VARI fits</h2>
<p>VARI Studio belongs to the first group: a 3D visualization, architecture and interior design studio in Cairo, working for projects in Germany, the Netherlands, Norway, Canada and the USA. If you need images built from your drawings, <a href="/en/work">see our work</a> or <a href="/en/contact">tell us about your project</a>.</p>
<h3>Sources (checked 2026-11-04)</h3>
<ul><li>Chaos / CGArchitect 3D Awards results 2024 and 2025: 3dawards.chaos.com</li><li>Chaos, "Chaos and Enscape merger: your questions answered": chaos.com/blog/chaos-and-enscape-merger-your-questions-answered</li><li>Epic Games, Twinmotion licence: twinmotion.com/license</li><li>Clutch, 3D rendering services category: clutch.co/agencies/product-design/3d-rendering-services</li><li>GoodFirms, 3D rendering companies: goodfirms.co/3d-rendering-companies</li></ul>$v$, $v$["Visualization studios make the images; software makers such as Chaos and Epic Games make the tools.", "Directories such as Clutch and GoodFirms are useful for breadth but need verification.", "Large architecture firms often run in-house visualization teams and outsource peaks.", "Decide which kind of company you need before you shortlist."]$v$::jsonb, $v$Top 3D Visualization Companies: Who Does What in 2026$v$, $v$The top 3D visualization companies are not all studios. A map of the industry: award-winning studios, the software makers behind them, and where to find talent.$v$, $v$top 3d visualization companies$v$, true, 754)
  on conflict (post_id, locale) do update set
    slug = excluded.slug, title = excluded.title, excerpt = excluded.excerpt, html = excluded.html, content = null,
